# Public site chrome (raynuv.com)

The look of `https://raynuv.com` is the **site-updater** design from PRs **#218–#226** (Syne + Source Serif, top nav, Status, CIO View fork cards, console screenshot, COM2 buddies, Stories mast, HDA tracker). That chrome lives on **`main`**.

**This rule always applies.** HDA / Everest / ISO agents historically rewrote `site/index.html` wholesale and deleted the CIO/Status chrome. Do not do that.

## Do

- **Patch lived strings in place** (status lede, hero proof, HDA tracker copy, story dates). Keep the HTML skeleton.
- Keep `site/hda.json` generated only by `./tools/sync-hda-site.sh` from `docs/hda.md` frontmatter.
- If a feature branch truncated `site/`, restore chrome from `origin/main` **surgically**. Do not merge all of `origin/main` into a hypervisor branch.
- After any `site/` edit, run `./tools/check-site-chrome.sh`.

## Do not

- Replace `site/index.html` wholesale while updating HDA, Everest, ISO, or SPA status.
- Delete `nav.site-nav`, `#status`, `#start-here` / `fork__card`, `#console`, `#buddies`, `ciospeak.html`, `com2.html`, `404.html`, `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, or responsive `site/assets/*.webp`.
- Restyle `site/index.html` / `site/styles.css` as part of hypervisor work. HDA closed-summit CSS (`.page-hda--closed`, `.section--hda-com2`) may be added; chrome CSS must stay.
- Point Cloudflare Git production at a feature branch.
- Claim `RAYNU-V-M7-ISO-INSTALL-OK` from nested QEMU, host tests, or CI.

## Required homepage landmarks

`site/index.html` must contain all of:

- `nav.site-nav` with links: Status, Console, Journey, Stories, Everest, Paper, **CIO View**
- HTML comment `REQUIRED SITE CHROME`
- `#status` (lived milestone copy — currently Everest closed on iron)
- `#start-here` with `fork__card` (CIO View + engineers)
- `#journey` with `.statband`
- `#console` (SPA screenshot)
- `#buddies` (Mr. COM2)

## Check

```bash
./tools/check-site-chrome.sh
./tools/sync-hda-site.sh --check
```
